# Addon release notes

A functional change to what a player can do updates `Addons/<Name>/RELEASE.md` in the same turn. Create the file on the first qualifying change. Use the version already in that addon's `Main.lua` (`VERSION`, same as the TOC `## Version`). Do not invent a version.

One entry per update. Newest first. A line that is only `---` separates entries so one note can be lifted out on its own.

Each entry has the version, a title, the local time of the update to the minute (`YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM`), and bullets. The version is the one in `Main.lua` when that update shipped. The same version can appear on more than one entry; the time separates them. A later change in a new minute is a new entry. Add bullets to an entry only when the change is still the same minute.

```markdown
## 0.3.4 — Sell leftover junk
2026-11-23 18:49

- Grey items in your bags sell in one pass at a vendor.
- Items you skip stay off the list until you add them back.

---

## 0.3.3 — Junk sales ledger
2026-11-23 18:40

- Each vendor trip records what sold and what it was worth.
```

## What goes in

- Player-facing behavior: a new action, a changed result, or a removed capability.
- Bullets say what the player can do. Short, plain language. No file names, functions, or implementation.
- A shared `Common/` change that alters player-facing behavior: update each addon whose players see it.

## What stays out

- Bug fixes, unless the user explicitly says to put that fix in the release notes.
- Visual changes (layout, color, spacing, icons, copy tweaks), unless the user explicitly says to put that change in the release notes.
- Developer-only work: dev mode, logging, slash debug, packaging, refactors, and comments.
